    {
      "domain": "destination-core",
      "subjectKey": "snowdonia",
      "field": "guide.highlights",
      "value": "Llanberis sits below Yr Wyddfa and within reach of the Glyderau, Tryfan and quieter northern ridges of Eryri National Park. The Llanberis route set makes those qualities concrete: “Yr Wyddfa via Llanberis Path” and “Pyg and Miners' Tracks Circuit” define different headline days, while “Tryfan North Ridge” offers another scale of outing. “Glyderau Traverse” and “Moel Eilio Circuit” extend the choice beyond one famous objective. Together, these Eryri / Snowdonia walks let a stay combine viewpoints, valleys and higher ground without treating every route as interchangeable.",
      "source": {
        "key": "snowdonia-authority",
        "url": "https://snowdonia.gov.wales/visit/walking/",
        "kind": "official"
      },
      "retrievedAt": "2026-07-25T20:00:00.000Z",
      "observedAt": "2026-07-25T20:00:00.000Z",
      "refreshAfter": "2027-07-25T20:00:00.000Z",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "domain": "destination-core",
      "subjectKey": "snowdonia",
      "field": "guide.terrain",
      "value": "Glaciated cwms, slate, volcanic rock and sharp ridges are packed into a small area, with rough stone pitching, boggy moor and hands-on scrambling often appearing on the same day. The published Llanberis walks move through that structure in distinct ways. “Moel Eilio Circuit” is the shortest listed option at about 5 hours from Llanberis; “Glyderau Traverse” is the largest commitment at about 9 hours. On Eryri / Snowdonia terrain, surface, exposure and ascent matter more than distance alone, so each route's description and difficulty should guide the choice.",
      "source": {
        "key": "snowdonia-authority",
        "url": "https://snowdonia.gov.wales/visit/walking/",
        "kind": "official"
      },
      "retrievedAt": "2026-07-25T20:00:00.000Z",
      "observedAt": "2026-07-25T20:00:00.000Z",
      "refreshAfter": "2027-07-25T20:00:00.000Z",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
    {
      "domain": "destination-core",
      "subjectKey": "snowdonia",
      "field": "guide.expectations",
      "value": "Bus and rail links are useful and paths are numerous, but the busiest summit lines crowd quickly; alternatives reward experienced walkers who can handle complex junctions, exposure and rapidly lowering cloud. Access around Llanberis is route-specific: starts include Llanberis Path gate at Victoria Terrace, Pen-y-Pass and A5 lay-by at Milestone Buttress. A Eryri / Snowdonia point-to-point walk needs transport at both ends, while an out-and-back still requires a firm turnaround time. These durations are planning estimates for the named routes, not live guarantees; check Llanberis weather, closures and seasonal services against the linked authority. Keep one of the listed Llanberis alternatives available when the principal route is unsuitable.",
      "source": {
        "key": "snowdonia-authority",
        "url": "https://snowdonia.gov.wales/visit/walking/",
        "kind": "official"
      },
      "retrievedAt": "2026-07-25T20:00:00.000Z",
      "observedAt": "2026-07-25T20:00:00.000Z",
